    {
      "id": "SBO-02",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-signed-branching-lambda-step",
      "title": "A nonzero smaller-group coefficient survives an ambient lowering",
      "hypotheses": "Both the current and lowered pair satisfy the rank, regularity and signature-gap assumptions. The current occurrence exists and λs−1/2 differs from all current μj. The smooth coefficient projection, the regular shifted tensor model, the compressed cofactor and fixed-parameter model equivalence are used.",
      "statement": "The scalar D_s on the projected corner multiplies Pη by Γ_s. The nonzero fixed overlap, the signed-form identity and the coefficient criterion give an occurrence of σ in π_s restricted to H.",
      "definitions": [
        "D_s is the unshifted product ∏k≠s(λk−λs); Γ_s is ∏j(μj−λs+1/2).",
        "The vectors are y₀=(p_s(e_zη))_z in the unshifted representation and b=r_s(e_zη) in the shifted ambient representation."
      ],
